course: dictionary
lesson: 3175
title: Words for rulers: empress
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An empress is a woman who rules an empire, which is a huge land with many people under one ruler. Read the words around the word to find this. «Empress Maria Theresa of Austria» tells you she was a woman ruler of a big country.
explain: The second meaning is about marriage. An empress can also be the wife of an emperor. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «She was the wife of the emperor» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Some clues show power, not just a title. «Empress Dowager Cixi was the most powerful person at the Qing court» tells you she held great power. An empress dowager is the mother or widow of an emperor, and the sentence shows what she could do.
fact: An empress is a woman who rules an empire.
fact: An empress can also be the wife of an emperor.
fact: «Queen Victoria» was Empress of India, so one woman can have more than one title.
fact: «Empress dowager» means the mother or widow of an emperor.
fact: In fairy tales, an empress is like a very powerful queen.
exercise: «Empress Maria Theresa of Austria» ruled a great country. What is an empress? | A leader of a small village | *A woman who rules an empire | A man who builds castles | A soldier in an army
exercise: An empress can be the wife of an emperor. In that meaning, what is an empress? | The baby of an emperor | The servant who cleans the palace | *The wife of an emperor | The name of a city
exercise: «Empress Dowager Cixi was the most powerful person at the Qing court.» What do the words «most powerful» tell you? | She was always sleepy | She lived in a boat | She was very short | *She held great power
test: «Empress dowager» means what? | A ship that sails across the sea | A teacher of history | A young girl who plays in the palace garden | *The mother or widow of an emperor
test: In a fairy tale, an empress is most like which of these? | A grey cloud | A tiny mouse | A talking tree | *A very powerful queen
exam: Which is true about an empress? | She is always a young child | *She rules an empire, or she is an emperor's wife | She is a kind of bird that lives by the sea | She can only live under the sea
